WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.760
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers&nbsp;
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér. Dr. Papers.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:10.440
Today I would like show you one&nbsp;
of my favorites - a work that I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.580
am really excited about. Now I&nbsp;
know, I know, you are saying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:21.120
Doc, you are always excited for these&nbsp;
papers, and yes, but today, extra excited.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:26.580
Because today we are going to talk&nbsp;
about how AI will supercharge school&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:33.660
and teaching. Most schools schools have tens,&nbsp;
or in Africa, unfortunately even hundreds of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:38.880
students for each teacher, and this makes&nbsp;
it very difficult to do this job well.&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:45.540
An ideal teacher would know all the answers&nbsp;
would have infinite patience, and an infinite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:51.540
amount of time for every student, and perhaps&nbsp;
would also be affordable for the students’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:59.040
families. But that is ridiculous, of course, such&nbsp;
a teacher has never existed before, until now.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:05.940
This is Khanmigo from Khan Academy. Khan&nbsp;
academy is an online set of a tools and lectures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:13.020
that help children study, and now it has been&nbsp;
supercharged by ChatGPT. Let’s marvel together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:18.780
at how this incredibly knowledgeable chatbot&nbsp;
can supercharge studying for children today.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:26.040
This is how it helps learning mathematics.&nbsp;
Hoo boy, so let’s just ask it to tell the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:32.820
answers and we are done! Well, look.&nbsp;
Oh yes, it knows all the answers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:40.200
but it would rather help us find out ourselves.&nbsp;
Loving it. Look at how well it slowly guides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:45.960
the student towards the right solution. And&nbsp;
if we don’t get even the first step right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:52.800
it does not get disappointed, it does not run out&nbsp;
of patience. It will be there to help us. Always.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:59.460
Now hold on to your papers, because this is&nbsp;
my favorite, and I am sure it will be yours&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:06.120
too in a moment. Yes, it also answers the&nbsp;
ultimate question that every student on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:12.180
planet has ever asked. And that is “Why&nbsp;
do I need to learn this?” Now, clearly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:18.240
every single Young Scholar has this question&nbsp;
in mind, but asking the teacher about it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:25.320
not always a good idea. But with an AI? Just&nbsp;
ask as much as you want! It’s not going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:30.600
get frustrated, and it has the knowledge&nbsp;
of the entire internet at its disposal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:36.120
What does that mean? It means that it can not&nbsp;
only explain what we are studying these for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:43.260
but you can even name your favorite activity, for&nbsp;
instance, soccer, and it will tell you exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:49.080
why mathematics could be useful for that.&nbsp;
Predicting player movements, data analytics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:57.000
and so on. This is fantastic, and I am 99% sure&nbsp;
it can do it for even more granular things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:03.780
not just mathematics in general. You will be able&nbsp;
to know exactly what a particular mathematical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:10.860
technique you are studying is good for. How it&nbsp;
can enrich your life. Now clearly, this is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:18.180
completely different level of teaching. I can only&nbsp;
wish I had a teacher like that. Wow. Imagine how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:23.400
excited the next generation of Young Scholars&nbsp;
will be with to study with tools like this!

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:30.060
So, what else can it do? Well, it also&nbsp;
quizzes you. And if you don’t know the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:36.060
answer, it doesn’t just plainly tell you the&nbsp;
answer, but it wants you to find out. First,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:41.280
you can even ask for a hint. These logs are&nbsp;
available for the teacher who can look up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:47.340
what the typical mistakes were and discuss&nbsp;
those during the next class. Or even ask&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:53.580
ChatGPT to do it in 10 seconds for all&nbsp;
the students. How incredible is that?

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:59.760
Get this, it can also debate you. If you&nbsp;
wish to start a debate about a sensitive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:05.220
